from pathlib import Path
p=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('current-page browser print/PDF','all-page PDF export; per-page raster EPS and current-page browser print').replace('Eleven automated tests','Twenty-four automated tests').replace('Native .inp read/write and legacy Noori/Lahori glyph encodings remain under development.', 'Native Unicode text recovery and limited same-length native text editing are implemented for the inspected AboutFaiz sample; general .inp layout decoding/writing and legacy Noori/Lahori glyph encodings remain under development.').replace('Pages are currently explicit; printing/export target the displayed page.', 'Pages are explicit for ordinary documents; the AboutFaiz linked story creates continuation pages automatically. PDF export covers all pages; browser print and HTML/EPS export target the displayed page.').replace('document record decoding is pending.', 'general document record decoding is pending. See research/ABOUTFAIZ-COMPATIBILITY.md for the verified import/write subset.');s+='\n### AboutFaiz reconstruction and native interoperability\n\nOpen the saved native sample through File > Open. Its full Unicode story and embedded banner are recovered into editable linked columns with colored headings. The sample profile uses Noto 8 pt as a substitute for native Faiz 12 pt; this is not exact native font/layout parity. examples/AboutFaiz-reconstruction.ipdoc is the editable two-page fixture.\n\nFile > Save as PDF exports every page, and File > Export Page as EPS exports the selected page. Both preserve the rendered Urdu as raster artwork. File > Export native INP preserves the original file, or patches same-length Unicode text edits while retaining native layout and formatting. It refuses layout/style changes, changed paragraph boundaries and resized stories. Reopen the native file on another device to restore its original bytes before native export.\n\nDocuments and original native bytes are stored in IndexedDB. The existing localStorage draft/tabs are migrated on first load. Native files remain local to this browser and are not sent to a server. Detailed evidence and limitations: research/ABOUTFAIZ-COMPATIBILITY.md.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('research/PARITY.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='\n## AboutFaiz import/export (2026-10-10)\n\nAdded full contiguous-Unicode story recovery for the inspected InPage300 sample, embedded JPEG recovery, manually inspected AboutFaiz geometry, colored paragraph runs in linked frames, continuation-page creation, all-page raster PDF, per-page raster EPS, IndexedDB persistence and native-source preservation. Native text edits that preserve character counts and paragraph boundaries can be patched into the original FAT sectors; tested with an actual web export reopened in InPage. General native record writing and exact Faiz shaping remain unresolved. See ABOUTFAIZ-COMPATIBILITY.md for the precise tested subset.\n\nThe earlier remaining-gap bullets describe the baseline before this addition. PDF now exports all pages; native text recovery/limited patching and colored frame runs now exist. Frame character formatting is still not a full rich-text editor, and continuation pagination is currently implemented for the AboutFaiz story profile.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
